[1556.109492, "o", "\u001b]3008;start=31582bdc-6dde-4aa6-9e44-e33a4cd69c8e;machineid=ec269368495231e336f7ec98aad6f10e;user=bandit10;hostname=gibson-0;bootid=b35b0f02-a9a4-4941-884c-a1ce6f7ec2e9;pid=00000000000000000003;type=command;cwd=/home/bandit10\u001b\\encode/decode data and print to standard output\r\nWith no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.\r\n\r\nThe data are encoded as described for the base64 alphabet in RFC\r\n3548.\r\nWhen decoding, the input may contain newlines in addition\r\nto the bytes of the formal base64 alphabet. Use --ignore-garbage\r\nto attempt to recover from any other non-alphabet bytes in the\r\nencoded stream.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mUsage:\u001b[0m base64 [OPTION]... [FILE]\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mArguments:\u001b[0m\r\n  [file]...  \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m-d\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--decode\u001b[0m          decode data [aliases: -D]\r\n  \u001b[1m-i\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--ignore-garbage\u001b[0m  when decoding, ignore non-alphabetic\r\n                        characters\r\n  \u001b[1m-w\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--wrap\u001b[0m <COLS>     wrap encoded lines after COLS character\r\n                        (default 76, 0 to disable wrapping)\r\n  \u001b[1m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--help\u001b[0m            Print help\r\n  \u001b[1m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--version\u001b[0m         Print version\r\n\u001b]3008;end=31582bdc-6dde-4aa6-9e44-e33a4cd69c8e;exit=success\u001b\\\u001b]3008;start=b070218c-f766-4657-b1e9-42aa763bf2f9;machineid=ec269368495231e336f7ec98aad6f10e;user=bandit10;hostname=gibson-0;bootid=b35b0f02-a9a4-4941-884c-a1ce6f7ec2e9;pid=00000000000000000003;type=shell;cwd=/home/bandit10\u001b\\\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;bandit10@bandit: ~\u0007\u001b[01;32mbandit10@bandit\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~\u001b[00m$ "]
